  "query_preview": "..\nAn area of monsoon showers is moving in, but the cloud tops on it \nare warming. So the forecast is for it to peter out after reaching \nGuam. Not a very high confidence forecast, since it may not even \nreach Guam. So the forecast for Guam has numerous showers tonight, a \nhigh PoP low QPF type scenario, while the CNMI has isolated. Starting\nSaturday, everyone adjusts back to scattered.\n\nThere isn't that much lightning around, and there isn't that much \npotential until you get way back near Yap. Nevertheless, went with a \nmoderate risk of lightning all week, just broad brushed it to cover \nany short lived convective flare-ups.",
